    "0e02e9d0f613633e4861fe41ec3d39f09004e733983cb7d264ed0fac67af2f6b": "##### Doctor\n\n- **Blocked when:** never — `fgos doctor` always runs every check and\n  reports the result; it never fails the invocation itself, only reports\n  individual checks as passing or not. Exit stays 0 because `fgctl\n  init|upgrade|repair` run it as their tail and mark the install degraded on\n  a non-zero exit; `--strict` is the opt-in that exits 1 when any check fails.\n- **What changes:** nothing — this is a read-only diagnostic. It never\n  writes a config file, never modifies a shell profile, and never installs\n  anything, even when a check reports a problem (`config-not-stale`\n  failing on a missing config file reports that plainly rather than\n  creating one).\n- **Side effects:** none.\n- **Afterwards:** the caller sees each named check (Data Dictionary #7) and\n  whether it passed, including enough detail to know what to do next (e.g.\n  which config settings are missing, or that `fgos setup` has not been run\n  yet).",
    "e271eeed7beea24622129fd4d840eb74128cf06b220440793a9ddeaca38c5f5b": "- **Blocked when:** never — `fgos doctor` always runs every check and\n  reports the result; it never fails the invocation itself, only reports\n  individual checks as passing or not. Exit stays 0 because `fgctl\n  init|upgrade|repair` run it as their tail and mark the install degraded on\n  a non-zero exit; `--strict` is the opt-in that exits 1 when any check fails.\n- **What changes:** nothing — this is a read-only diagnostic. It never\n  writes a config file, never modifies a shell profile, and never installs\n  anything, even when a check reports a problem (`config-not-stale`\n  failing on a missing config file reports that plainly rather than\n  creating one).\n- **Side effects:** none.\n- **Afterwards:** the caller sees each named check (Data Dictionary #7) and\n  whether it passed, including enough detail to know what to do next (e.g.\n  which config settings are missing, or that `fgos setup` has not been run\n  yet).",
    "2ca5f16c0ec10dd39d43e98522ab2c2bad332e112e2da370d92a38eb62069473": "## Dependency Upgrade Discipline\n\n- **RUL107 (a third-party crate that a component's contract rests on is pinned exactly and has an upgrade record and acceptance tests; 2026-10-23).** Such a crate (the YAML parser under `fgos-yaml-doc`, the JSON Schema validator under `fgos-config`) is pinned with `=` in the root `[workspace.dependencies]`, never a range; the package that relies on it carries an `upgrade-record.md` (what was read, transitive crates, audit coverage, deny result, known defects with their guards and upstream links, bump procedure, owner sign-off) and acceptance tests that fail when a bump changes a behavior the contract depends on, including one test per known defect that fails when upstream fixes it. A bump lands only when those tests pass and the record is updated. Backlog item p-3c9e7a15 extends this to every dependency. Records: `packages/yaml-doc/upgrade-record.md`, `packages/config/upgrade-record.md`.\n\nThe vendored YAML parser upgrade and advisory procedure is owned by [Vendored YAML parser maintenance](decisions/vendored-yaml-parser.md).",
    "9b76e5e7e2e62bb486cac01fa6da0b59f5fc7198434824cca28ae68c81702adc": "- **RUL107 (a third-party crate that a component's contract rests on is pinned exactly and has an upgrade record and acceptance tests; 2026-10-23).** Such a crate (the YAML parser under `fgos-yaml-doc`, the JSON Schema validator under `fgos-config`) is pinned with `=` in the root `[workspace.dependencies]`, never a range; the package that relies on it carries an `upgrade-record.md` (what was read, transitive crates, audit coverage, deny result, known defects with their guards and upstream links, bump procedure, owner sign-off) and acceptance tests that fail when a bump changes a behavior the contract depends on, including one test per known defect that fails when upstream fixes it. A bump lands only when those tests pass and the record is updated. Backlog item p-3c9e7a15 extends this to every dependency. Records: `packages/yaml-doc/upgrade-record.md`, `packages/config/upgrade-record.md`.",
    "46972cdc9219aa145329eb354726b98ab0d4fa7915c3e96b6517e3a0f19bc3d9": "## Dependency Upgrade Discipline\n\n- **RUL107 (a third-party crate that a component's contract rests on is pinned exactly and has an upgrade record and acceptance tests; 2026-10-23).** Such a crate (the YAML parser under `fgos-yaml-doc`, the JSON Schema validator under `fgos-config`) is pinned with `=` in the root `[workspace.dependencies]`, never a range; the package that relies on it carries an `upgrade-record.md` (what was read, transitive crates, audit coverage, deny result, known defects with their guards and upstream links, bump procedure, owner sign-off) and acceptance tests that fail when a bump changes a behavior the contract depends on, including one test per known defect that fails when upstream fixes it. A bump lands only when those tests pass and the record is updated. Backlog item p-3c9e7a15 extends this to every dependency. Records: `packages/yaml-doc/upgrade-record.md`, `packages/config/upgrade-record.md`.\n\n- **RUL108 (every YAML parse goes through the native door: one Rust parser behind `src/util/yaml.mjs`; supersedes RUL101; 2026-10-23).** `fgos-yaml-doc` (parser `saphyr-parser` =0.2.2, pinned and vendored under RUL107 (a third-party crate under a component contract is pinned exactly with an upgrade record and acceptance tests)) is the only YAML parser. `parseYaml(text, { filename })` keeps its signature and calls the addon's `yaml` namespace with the `tool` profile; objects reach JavaScript from JSON text, so a `__proto__` key stays an own key; a Rust panic becomes the named refusal `yaml-internal-error` and never aborts Node. There is no JavaScript fallback: a process that cannot load the addon fails every YAML read with the door's named error (`git-addon-unavailable` or `git-addon-not-shipped`). `package.json#dependencies` stays empty. `test/architecture.test.mjs` fails on any YAML library import anywhere, the door included; `.github/cargo-deny.toml` bans the other Rust YAML crates. Authority for what YAML means: `docs/platform/yaml-document/spec.md`.\n\nThe former vendored-parser upgrade procedure is retained only as superseded history below; current parser maintenance follows `packages/yaml-doc/upgrade-record.md` and RUL107.",
    "d17ec9a9681777775fe057074ba928ff335b23be896b99ce750f00927f225ab7": "- **RUL108 (every YAML parse goes through the native door: one Rust parser behind `src/util/yaml.mjs`; supersedes RUL101; 2026-10-23).** `fgos-yaml-doc` (parser `saphyr-parser` =0.2.2, pinned and vendored under RUL107 (a third-party crate under a component contract is pinned exactly with an upgrade record and acceptance tests)) is the only YAML parser. `parseYaml(text, { filename })` keeps its signature and calls the addon's `yaml` namespace with the `tool` profile; objects reach JavaScript from JSON text, so a `__proto__` key stays an own key; a Rust panic becomes the named refusal `yaml-internal-error` and never aborts Node. There is no JavaScript fallback: a process that cannot load the addon fails every YAML read with the door's named error (`git-addon-unavailable` or `git-addon-not-shipped`). `package.json#dependencies` stays empty. `test/architecture.test.mjs` fails on any YAML library import anywhere, the door included; `.github/cargo-deny.toml` bans the other Rust YAML crates. Authority for what YAML means: `docs/platform/yaml-document/spec.md`.",
    "fa0f95653d8142080a30ff8f7b25b061f1bc332c4cbf9ff48ef4d56bc3d3b38c": "## 10. Non-Goals\n\nPackaging-distribution does not define:\n\n- workflow semantics after a correct local runtime has been selected;\n- shared gateway/dashboard serving many projects;\n- confinement policy behavior beyond doctor/fix readiness checks;\n- host invocation provider routing inside the selected runtime.",
