e capability) left unbuilt on the Unit; `dispatch decide` still has none.\n- **RUL89 (`fgos workflow start --units <file>` runs a list of Units as a one-off Workflow, 2026-10-14; decision 0061).** The units file (YAML/JSON, `{ id?, title?, units }` or a list of Units, `src/workflow/units-source.mjs`) becomes one step per Unit, `dependsOn` becomes step dependencies, a Unit id must be a safe branch-name segment, and the workflow id is `units/<id|basename>`. The `units-file` source is passed by the loader to the validator, never read from the data, and is the only source whose unit templates may carry `prefer`. `--seats` is refused with `--units`. `--effort <level>` (`low|medium|high|max`, otherwise refused before a run exists) becomes an override `{ reasoningEffort, origin: 'human-cli' }` for every unit, stored in `workflow.start` and reused on resume. A unit template's `persona` travels on the Unit (provenance `unit`); persona overrides remain only for `--seats` seats. A writing unit that stands on exactly one writing ancestor (directly or through read-only units; an integrate step cuts the path) starts its worktree from that unit's branch sha; a file with a writing unit standing on two or more writing units is refused at start; nothing is merged automatically and `workflow status` lists `writeBranches` (branch, worktree, base). A unit that wrote outside its scope (reported by its commit, or found in its branch diff outside `writeScope`) ends `findings` (`out-of-scope-writes`); a unit standing on that branch inherits only the out-of-scope paths the branch carries; an integrate step whose dependency is flagged fails and merges nothing. A writing unit that gets no worktree of its own (base branch gone, worktree creation failed) fails and never runs in the shared checkout. Residual: a writing unit after an integrate step still starts from the main checkout's HEAD, not the integrate target.\n- **RUL90 (the raw dispatch doors are removed; dispatch is the lower layer and f