unt of a unit run; the pin is hard and never bypasses the lease, 2026-10-14).** `fgos run --account <id>`, or an `account` key on an `--override` object (one shape; a Unit carries no account), pins a provider account (`src/runner/execution/account-pin.mjs`). `bind()` pins it on each seat its override reaches whose bound executor's provider (normalized as the lease does) lists it in `providers.<provider>.accounts`: `binding.account = { provider, id }`, `provenance.account = { value, source: override:<origin> }`. A seat on another provider (a checker must use another family), an executor without an account list, and a tool or inline binding bind unpinned with `provenance.account.skipped { reason, detail }`; the pin never chooses the executor (pair it with `--provider`); a malformed id is refused (`account-pin-invalid`), and an inherited object key is never an account id. Before the unit run exists the seats are dry-bound as the run would bind them (`simulateUnitBindings` with the run's overrides): a pin no seat takes, or a quarantined account (the message names `until` and the reason code), is refused. A pinned seat is dispatched with the inventory narrowed to its account (`configPinnedToAccount`, as RUL79 (`fgos dispatch probe-account`: one account, every CLI) does), so the lease, quarantine and governance apply unchanged. A provider limit on a pinned seat ends it (`fallbackExhausted.reason: account-pinned`, `retryStopped` on the attempt): no account rotation, no executor failover. `--account` is refused with `--resume`; a resumed run keeps its bindings' account and is refused while that account is quarantined. Left open: the login store per CLI (RUL80 (an account is chosen first, then a CLI)) is checked only by the lease at dispatch, after the unit run exists; `capacityProviderOf` derives the provider from the executor entry and can differ from the lease's for an executor that declares no `providerModel` (every configured executor declares one); `fgos workflow start