cord per project at the main checkout's `.fgos` (not event truth, never replayed, never pushed). First slice imports only `fgos-process`, `fgos-holder-lock`, `fgos-durable-file` and `fgos-identity`; its core crate `fgos-mailbox-core` depends on serde alone. Never owns writer identity (Session Identity), process liveness (Process Facts & Control), the main-checkout `.fgos` resolver (the host), pane access (Terminal-control), typing or screen reading (Agent protocol; a later part), hook installation (the setup installer), locks (Holder-lock), communication authorization or case budgets (coordination foundation), or steering a Unit attempt (the runner). Rust crates `fgos-mailbox-core` and `fgos-mailbox` (planned: `packages/mailbox/rust`). | [agent-mailbox/spec.md](agent-mailbox/spec.md) |",
