dge, Learning, And Documentation Registry | Retrospective learning, doc registry, end-user docs index, trace/evolve signals. | Knowledge and docs registry docs |\n| Observe (Metrics & Friction) | Measurement and friction tracking across substrate entities (cases, runs, sessions, friction, snapshots). Owned in Rust (`packages/observe/rust`), native routing. | [observe/spec.md](observe/spec.md) |\n| Convention (Executable Names & Placement) | Platform-core authority for deterministic artifact names, repository-relative placement, path classification, and conformance checking. Implemented; owns no state and depends only on `fgos-host-runtime`. | [convention/spec.md](convention/spec.md) |\n| Identity (foundation; today the local session writer id) | Foundation authority for identities, today for \"who is the writer of this process\" (`{id, source}`). One implementation, the Rust crate `fgos-identity` (`packages/identity/rust`, native verb `fgos identity`); Observe calls it in process, Node through the facade `src/util/session-identity.mjs` over the combined addon's `sessionIdentity` namespace. Also mints the writer id of an attempt (`att-<attemptId>`) and carries the launcher's env scrub the gate applies. Also mints and reads the machine id (`<stateRoot>/machine-id`, optional `machine-alias`; `fgos identity machine`, doctor row `identity-machine-id`) and derives the machine handle; also reads and, on an explicit `fgos identity project --init`, mints the project id (the tracked file `.fgos/project.json`; doctor row `identity-project-id`; the provider reads the Git component for the trusted main root and the remote default branch); the one validator of the id shape lives here. The host provider sits behind the default cargo feature `provider` (needs `fgos-host-runtime`, `fgos-holder-lock`, `fgos-convention`, `fgos-git`); Event Store and the node addon depend on the library with `default-features = false`, so the event log never pulls the host runtime. The process-tree ada