e gate holds the attempt lock and outlives a dead supervisor), applies the environment scrub and the attempt writer id, reaps every orphan with `waitpid(-1)` for the whole attempt, enforces the hard ceiling (SIGTERM, `dispatch.gateKillGraceMs`, SIGKILL) on its own clock and publishes `gate-exit.json` once the domain is empty. `fgos internal gate`; same crate and spec as the supervisor. | [run-supervisor/spec.md](run-supervisor/spec.md#5-supervisor-and-gate) |\n| Agent protocol (L3) | Pure per-CLI adapters (claude, codex, agy, pi, omp) that read what an agent CLI showed (capture tail, exit, outbox) and name the result (`completed`, `blocked(login\\|trust-dialog\\|usage-limit)`, `needs-human`, `exited`); decide stdin policy and the activity source for idle. Never builds argv (that stays with the executor configuration through `resolveExecutorCommand`), never retries, no dependency on terminal-control, locks or attempts. Direct and terminal adapters; the terminal ones read the pane through `AgentIo` (`screen`, `inspect`) wired by the supervisor to terminal-control. Crate `fgos-agent-protocol` (`packages/agent-protocol/rust`). | [agent-protocol/spec.md](agent-protocol/spec.md) |\n| Agent Mailbox (L4, signed at G0 on 2026-10-20; implementation not started) | Single authority for \"how a message from one agent session is placed into the context of the right live head of a CLI on this machine, with an honest delivery report, and never as the user's input\": the envelope, the delivery state machine (`recorded`, `in-flight`, `offered`, `refused`), the registry of heads (name, per-process generation, process `Record`), the channel-protection policies, the peer frame, and the per-CLI hook payload shape and non-terminal wake channels (the Claude Code scoped socket, `codex queue`). Recipients are independently started interactive heads, never a runner Unit attempt, a subagent or a teammate. Owns one runtime-state record per project at the main checkout's `.fgos` (not event truth